## Supervisor decision on the round-1 BLOCKER
The production ClientServer server ROUTER uses HANDOVER (`ZLinkChannelBundleFactory.cs:55`, `router.Options.Handover = true`);
the malformed-control fixture's raw ROUTER (`ClientServerChannelRuntimeTests.cs:1774`) uses the Core default REJECT, which the
product never runs. Under REJECT a same-RID reconnect arriving before the old pipe's termination is rejected by design and the
request submitted right after the DEALER's READY edge times out — the removed manual reconnect loop had masked that by
re-admitting repeatedly (a workaround). The REJECT reconnect semantics (D-B104 spec gap #1: should a REJECT ROUTER close the
duplicate so the DEALER auto-reconnects? does the DEALER's READY edge imply ROUTER admission?) are recorded as a Core/spec
follow-up for the user, NOT to be solved in the framework or the fixture. Therefore: align the fixture's raw ROUTER with the
production policy (HANDOVER), via the same option the factory sets, and keep the assertions unchanged. Class A (test double
aligned to the real configuration), with a note in the summary.

